INT: It was closed by--

AH: By my father. It could no longer function. What my father did, he took-- [PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS] wooden post cards from the First World War. And he used to have a little tray and sell it in the cafes where the Germans were sitting to get some money.

INT: Did your father ever have plans to escape, to go to East Poland or somewhere else-- with all of you?

